## The Bug

There are actually two problems:

**1. Wrong comparison operator (the stated bug):**
```javascript
if (decoded.exp < Date.now() / 1000)  // strict < accepts exp === now
```
Should be `<=` to reject tokens expiring exactly at the current time (per [RFC 7519](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519#section-4.1.4): "on or after which the JWT MUST NOT be accepted").

**2. The manual check is redundant and error-prone:**
`jwt.verify()` already throws a `TokenExpiredError` when `exp <= now`. The manual check after verify is dead code that duplicates (incorrectly) what the library already does correctly. It also only runs if verify *succeeds*, which means an expired token would have been caught by verify first anyway — but if you ever disabled expiry checking via `{ ignoreExpiration: true }`, this buggy guard would be your only line of defense.

**3. The catch block swallows all error types** — a `TokenExpiredError`, a malformed token, and a missing `JWT_SECRET` all return the same generic message.

## Fix

```javascript
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');

function authMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];

  if (!token) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'No token provided' });
  }

  try {
    // jwt.verify rejects exp <= now per RFC 7519 — no manual check needed
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    req.user = decoded;
    next();
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name === 'TokenExpiredError') {
      return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });
    }
    if (err.name === 'JsonWebTokenError') {
      return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
    }
    // Covers NotBeforeError and unexpected failures (e.g. missing JWT_SECRET)
    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Authentication error' });
  }
}

module.exports = authMiddleware;
```

Key changes: removed the redundant/buggy manual expiry check, and split the catch into three cases so expired tokens, malformed tokens, and server misconfigurations each get an appropriate response code and message.
